l graph\",\"observation\":\"The curve positions and equilibrium labels are clear and readable.\",\"interpretation\":\"The diagram is internally readable and assessable, but the market outcome shown is inconsistent with a drought reducing wheat harvests under unchanged demand.\",\"uncertain\":false}],\"summary\":\"The student’s diagram is clear and fully readable. It shows an unchanged demand curve, two supply curves with S2 to the right of S1, and equilibria shifting from E1 to E2 with lower price (P2 below P1) and higher quantity (Q2 right of Q1). So the diagram depicts a supply increase/rightward shift rather than the required supply contraction from a drought.\"}"
